      },
      "message": "fix(sim): credit an edge-break record only within its op's stated width\n\nThe program sim forgave convicted columns down to a cached edge-break\nrecord's depth, and a project file's record could state any depth - a\nhand edit could hide a real gouge under an inflated bevel. Each op's\nrecords are now held to the break width its own params state\n(Chamfer2D / Deburr `width`); a wider record, or one on a kind that\ndeclares no break, is dropped with a logged warning and its columns are\njudged against the sharp model.\n\nPinned by edge_break_bound::{an_inflated_record_no_longer_forgives_a_deeper_cut,\nan_unedited_file_still_credits_its_own_break, the_bound_reads_the_ops_own_width}.\n\nFixes #529\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
